 independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ | $0.75$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.7$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=3)=f(0,3)=0.15.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(3)=0.25\\cdot 0.3=0.075.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=0,Y=3)\\ne P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143334/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143334"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162901/selection/d08818d9751d48a05f01ba37497d3da27fbe70f705234d8e06d8830c6b479721" :answer/id #uuid "0cb942e6-aced-5725-82f8-561f2901283e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162901/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "db97b7d2-8393-525a-942e-e16082a21dfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162901/selection/91afb9a0ba928957f30252e15bfbaf7fa3834bb4fbb0b0864156247fdeeccc36" :answer/id #uuid "88d9904c-d607-553b-bef2-5713e95b316d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answ