)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our random variables are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,-1) & ={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-1) \\\\ P(X=2,Y=-1) & =P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=-1) \\\\ 0.03 & =0.1\\cdot P(Y=-1) \\\\ P(Y=-1) & =\\frac{0.03}{0.1} \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-162901/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "900dcaf8-da39-5654-96cd-6aec89e379c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162901"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149651/selection/d3af39c27478149ba159361f1ea28392bb5715ba1d71d02f3a1b19368ff06f61" :answer/id #uuid "85edc7a8-b7a4-5f74-9c49-a752fa07ab43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149651/selection/3cbdf95cfd5e40a66d9c06a25fae4f2b1ebc35cb68cd1a8c8fced199bacffd13" :answer/id #uuid "985c4365-c0d4-5fa0-a55e-c41f1c0be7b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Impossible to determine using the given information." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149651/selection/390a057aab4ff928869e287dd27def5e0b317f10b84e391f0a09bc7e70ff74fb" :answer/id #uuid "c5c27e92-c78e-5458-87f4-43ba0f932f34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149651/selection/514e33c9b858c825c428dba350b8264609585198d932cd8e87f5a118b0dd2847" :answer/id #uuid "94026d59-3505-5d93-9b18-c94e762b7e59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149651/selection/44cb327747caefbcb4ffb32f5badaa0166b5e979cc6862940f9cde0823f1defc" :answer/id #uuid "74109c17-3de0-5383-a632-1aca9994842e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.09" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149651/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4e51138-4831-5e32-b9c2-6e2ce3977be0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :a