 | $0.5$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.35$ |" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our discrete random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & ={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) \\\\  & =0.4\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-143317/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "900dcaf8-da39-5654-96cd-6aec89e379c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143317"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162899/selection/77ecb83eade0a71c8fc58d1bc109d2da2e721f0d3bc137ebdd193c4c561aa82b" :answer/id #uuid "8471a0da-38ed-533c-a0ee-dfea941591d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162899/selection/390a057aab4ff928869e287dd27def5e0b317f10b84e391f0a09bc7e70ff74fb" :answer/id #uuid "386ab619-11e7-5250-82d0-3f61753dfed6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162899/selection/8cdaa067f375a830d5b1e57b5029529ea90227c752cbf890839edae4bfd1a326" :answer/id #uuid "9ad30b59-400a-54a6-b597-1ecd5088d3cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162899/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "07589031-8aa9-52a6-a219-8e709b861ffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162899/selection/ad362f3c4852a28674b9519bed1fece599a9efb1cccb073912f82948eef407fa" :answer/id #uuid "e1918e45-b4b0-5463-ac9f-bbdf240c502e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162899/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "66b823c6-b423-5ba0-ab6b-7fbdb48acfb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162899/selection/390a057aab4ff928869e287dd27def5e0b317f10b84e391f0a09bc7e70ff74fb" :answer-field/choices ["q-162899/selection/77ecb83eade0a71c8fc58d1bc109d2da2e721f0d3bc137ebdd193c4c561aa82b" "q-162899/selection/390a057aab4ff928869e287dd27def5e0b317f10b84e391f0a09bc7e70ff74fb" "q-162899/selection/8cdaa067f375a830d5b1e57b5029529ea90227c752cbf890839edae4bfd1a326" "q-162899/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-162899/selection/ad362f3c4852a28674b9519bed1fece599a9efb1cccb073912f82948eef407fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162899" :question/id #uuid "76a9bd4c-2981-511b-8af4-34bbe22f3289" :question/math-academy-id "q-162899" :question/problem "The partially complete joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $∗$ | $0.35$ | $∗$ |\n| $X=2$ | $∗$ | $0.25$ | $?$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $P(X=2),$ rounded to two decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our random variables are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,1) & ={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) \\\\ P(X=2,Y=1) & =P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=1) \\\\ 0.25 & =P(X=2)\\cdot 0.6 \\\\ P(X=2) & =\\frac{0.25}{0.6} \\\\  & ≈0.42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-162899/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "900dcaf8-da39-5654-96cd-6aec89e379c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162899"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12464"] :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.24$ | $0.06$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.56$ | $0.14$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n| | $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | |  | | $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.8$ | $0.2$ | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.8$ | $0.2$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P({X = 0}, {Y = 0}) = P(X=0) \\cdot P(Y=0)$\n\n- $P({X = x}, {Y = y}) = P(X=x) \\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\n- $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x, y) = f_X(x) \\cdot f_Y (y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y (y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P({X = 0}, {Y = 0}) = f(0,0) = 0.24.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0) \\cdot P(Y=0) = f_X(0) \\cdot f_Y(0) = 0.3 \\cdot 0.8 = 0.24. \\quad {\\color{green}\\checkmark}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0) & =0.56=0.7\\cdot 0.8={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(0) & ✓ \\\\ f(0,1) & =0.06=0.3\\cdot 0.2={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,1) & =0.14=0.7\\cdot 0.2={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P({X = x}, {Y = y}) = P(X=x) \\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12462"] :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.28$ | $0.12$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.42$ | $0.18$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P({X = 0}, {Y = 0}) = P(X=0) \\cdot P(Y=0)$\n\n- $P({X = x}, {Y = y}) = P(X=x) \\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\n- $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x, y) = f_X(x) \\cdot f_Y (y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y (y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.28$ | $0.12$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.42$ | $0.18$ | $0.6$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.7$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P({X = 0}, {Y = 0}) = f(0,0) = 0.28.$ Likewise, \n\n$$\nP(X=0) \\cdot P(Y=0) = f_X(0) \\cdot f_Y(0) = 0.4 \\cdot 0.7 = 0.28. \\quad {\\color{green}\\checkmark}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,1) & =0.12=0.4\\cdot 0.3={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,0) & =0.42=0.6\\cdot 0.7={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(0) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,1) & =0.18=0.6\\cdot 0.3={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P({X = x}, {Y = y}) = P(X=x) \\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12463"] :question/problem "The marginal mass functions of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(4,2).$\n\n| | $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | |  | | $y$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $4$ |  |  |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ |  |  |" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
